original figures are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International. This includes data/, docs/, environment/, source_data/,
reference_outputs/, the root README and citation metadata, and non-code
materials within code/. See LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0 for the full legal text.
Provide appropriate attribution, identify changes, and retain the license
information as required by that license. Recommended citation information
is in CITATION.cff.

2. Original software: MIT

Original analysis scripts, experiment programs, PsychoPy Builder files,
and code notebooks under code/ are licensed under the MIT License.
Notebook code is covered by MIT; embedded third-party material retains its
own terms, and original embedded data, figures, and explanatory prose are
covered by CC BY 4.0. See LICENSE-MIT for the full license text.

3. Third-party and excluded materials

The licenses above apply only to rights the authors hold. They do not
